{{define "31-language-mix.tmpl"}}
{{with .Collaboration}}
{{with .LanguageMix}}
<div class="metric-story">
  <h3>Tech stack fingerprint</h3>
  <p class="muted">
    Programming language distribution derived from diff-shape data &mdash; file extensions
    and line counts only, never file contents. This shows <strong>exposure</strong>, not
    proficiency or skill level. Languages with less than 3&percnt; share are folded into
    Other to protect niche internal technology.
  </p>

  {{shareBarSVG $}}

  <p class="caption">basis: diff lines across <strong>{{.PRCount}} merged pull request{{if ne .PRCount 1}}s{{end}}</strong> ({{.TotalLines}} lines)</p>

  <p class="limit">
    <strong>Limit:</strong> this is a proxy for the languages a developer has been
    exposed to, not a measure of expertise. A repository&rsquo;s language distribution
    reflects team conventions and project requirements, not individual preference or
    skill. File extensions tell you about file types, not code quality or depth of
    engagement.
  </p>
</div>
{{end}}
{{end}}
{{end}}